@page "/reference/api"

@* The API reference (ADR-0201, ADR-0110), a reference page: every public type of the family's packages,
   read by the build from the assemblies a release ships, by product in ADR-0042's order. The contract is
   listed under each product; what is public and not the contract is listed apart, at the end, as what may
   change in any version. A type's name opens its API table, the one the topic pages place. *@
<DocsPage Title="API reference"
          Lead="Every public type of the family's packages, by product and package. A type's name opens its table: a component's parameters, events and methods, a type's constructors, properties and methods. What is public and not the contract is listed apart, at the end.">
    <ReferenceAsOf>
        Read from the shipped assemblies the site was built with, each type's description from the documentation its
        package ships.
    </ReferenceAsOf>
    <p class="docs-reference-asof">
        A type is public when a Consumer, a Chrome or a sibling product uses it, or when a public signature names it;
        everything else is internal. Each package also declares its public members in <code>PublicAPI.Shipped.txt</code>
        and <code>PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt</code> beside its project, and a build that adds or removes one without
        declaring it fails, so a change to the surface shows in review. Decided in
        <a href="@DocsBuild.BlobUrl(ApiSurface.RecordPath)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ADR-0201</a>.
    </p>

    <DocsSection Title="ExGrid">
        <ApiPackages Product="ExGrid" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="ExSheet">
        <ApiPackages Product="ExSheet" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="The Snapshot">
        <ApiPackages Product="The Snapshot" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="ExPivot">
        <ApiPackages Product="ExPivot" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="ExChart">
        <ApiPackages Product="ExChart" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="Not the contract">
        <p>
            <b>@ApiSurface.NotTheContract.</b> These are public because Razor places only a public component, or because
            the grid's own script calls them, and each is hidden from a Consumer's editor
            (<code>[EditorBrowsable(EditorBrowsableState.Never)]</code>). A Consumer, a Chrome or a Wrapper does not use
            them: the parts a product's components render themselves, the methods and payloads of the grid's script, and
            the types only those name. Making them internal can be reconsidered before 1.0.
        </p>
        <ApiNotContract />
    </DocsSection>
</DocsPage>
